//
// loft#1211's NEGATIVE half.  `const` binds through a NULL DISCHARGE that sits INSIDE an
// assignment place, exactly as it binds through the dense spelling one field over.
//
// `(Const-Value)` (@FR-Const-Value) opts a binding OUT of every through-write, and the rule
// is about the write's ROOT: `h.i?.x = …` reaches `h` for the same reason `h.i.x = …` does,
// because a discharge changes what a read ANSWERS and not which binding a write travels to.
// So this is enforcement that was missing at a site, not a rule being extended — the target
// `.x` is an interior place (`H-View`) and the write itself stays legal on a non-`const`
// receiver, which `1211b` scores.
//
// The defect: `lhs_base_var` walks a place to find the binding a write reaches and had no arm
// for either shape a discharge lowers to, so a place ROOTED in one answered `u16::MAX` — no
// binding at all — and `validate_write` had nothing to check.  A `const` parameter was mutated
// in silence and the CALLER saw the new value, on both backends, with no diagnostic.
//
// The dense control — `i: Ic1211` and `h.i.x = 99`, refused throughout — is what named the
// discharge as the cause rather than `const` itself, and it is deliberately NOT a cell here.
// Scored in this file it makes the file exit 1 on the pre-fix build too, which leaves
// `falsify.sh` reading INERT on every channel it has (measured: `1|0|none|none` both trees,
// both backends) and moves the whole answer into a diagnostic COUNT only `tests/wrap.rs` can
// see.  It is not needed for what it was there for either: a build where `const` dies outright
// leaves this file's own `@EXPECT_ERROR` unmatched, so the harness fails it anyway.  Measured
// by hand instead, both backends, on the pre-fix build and on this one — "Cannot modify const
// parameter 'h'" in all four runs.
//
// In its own file because a firing `@EXPECT_ERROR` stops the file before it runs; the writes
// that must still go through are `1211b-a-place-behind-an-interior-discharge-is-written.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: c3226d07 — interpret exit 0 -> 1, native exit 0 -> 1.  On the control the file
//   compiles and RUNS with no diagnostic at all: the `const` parameter is mutated and the run
//   reports nothing, which is the defect.  `make falsify` reads that pair but cannot render a
//   verdict for an annotation-scored file — a passing `@EXPECT_ERROR` guard exits 1, which its
//   exit channel reads as "THIS TREE IS NOT CLEAN".  The gating channel is `check_diagnostics`
//   in `tests/wrap.rs`: the `@EXPECT_ERROR` above goes unmatched on the control, because there
//   is nothing to match.
//   HOLDS: assertions, leak, panic, free-refusal are equal on both trees. Falsify prints only
//   the channels that MOVE and requires HERE to be clean, so each of those is clean on both.
//   The native side was not scored in this sweep.

struct Ic1211 { x: integer }
struct Nc1211 { i: Ic1211? }

// The cell.  A discharge INTERIOR to the place, on a `const` receiver.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot modify const parameter 'h1211n'
fn n1211_touch(h1211n: const Nc1211) {
  h1211n.i?.x = 99;
}

fn main() {
  n1211_touch(Nc1211 { i: Ic1211 { x: 1 } });
}
